      "content": "# How to Send Files Between Devices Without Signing Up\n\nNeed to quickly send a file or message to another device? No email, no cloud storage accounts, no sign-up forms. Just instant, encrypted sharing with a simple room code or QR scan.\n\n## Why Send Files Without Accounts?\n\n### Benefits of Account-Free Sharing\n\n- **Instant**: No registration, verification, or login\n- **Private**: No data stored on servers\n- **Simple**: Six-digit code or QR scan\n- **Secure**: End-to-end encryption\n- **Free**: No subscriptions or limits\n- **Cross-platform**: Works on any device with a browser\n\n### When You Need It\n\n**Quick transfers**:\n- Photos from phone to laptop\n- Documents to colleague's device\n- Files at a meeting\n- Emergency file sharing\n\n**Privacy-conscious**:\n- Sensitive documents\n- Personal photos\n- Confidential business files\n- Medical records\n\n**One-time shares**:\n- No ongoing relationship\n- Temporary collaboration\n- Event-based sharing\n\n## How Room Code Sharing Works\n\n### Basic Process\n\n1. **Sender creates room**: Gets 6-digit code\n2. **Sender shares code**: Via voice, text, or screen\n3. **Receiver enters code**: Joins same room\n4. **Transfer happens**: Files and messages flow securely\n5. **Done**: Room ends when devices disconnect\n\n### Security Layer\n\nAll data is:\n- **Encrypted on your device** before sending\n- **Transmitted as ciphertext** through servers\n- **Decrypted only on receiver's device**\n- **Never stored unencrypted** anywhere\n\n**Encryption standard**: ECDH P-256 key exchange with AES-GCM 256-bit encryption\n\nServers see only:\n- Room codes (temporary, random)\n- Encrypted data (unreadable)\n- Connection status\n\nServers cannot see:\n- File names\n- File contents\n- Your messages\n- Any metadata\n\n## Step-by-Step: Sending Files\n\n### Method 1: Room Codes\n\n**On sender's device**:\n\n1. Open the Share tool\n2. Click **\"Send\"**\n3. Note the 6-digit code (e.g., 482901)\n4. Share code with receiver (say it, text it, show screen)\n5. Wait for \"Connected\" status\n6. Type messages or select files to send\n7. Watch progress bar\n8. Done when transfer completes\n\n**On receiver's device**:\n\n1. Open the Share tool\n2. Click **\"Receive\"**\n3. Enter the 6-digit code\n4. Click **\"Join\"**\n5. Wait for \"Connected\" status\n6. Received files/messages appear automatically\n7. Click **\"Download\"** for files\n8. Done!\n\n### Method 2: QR Codes\n\n**Faster for nearby devices**:\n\n1. **Sender**: Click \"Send\" → QR code appears\n2. **Receiver**: Scan QR with phone camera\n3. Browser opens and auto-joins room\n4. Starts transferring immediately\n\n**Best for**:\n- Phone ↔ laptop\n- Same room sharing\n- Quick one-offs\n\n## What You Can Share\n\n### Text Messages\n\n- Quick notes\n- URLs\n- Passwords (securely)\n- Code snippets\n- Instructions\n\n**How**:\n1. Type in text box\n2. Click \"Send Text\"\n3. Appears on other device instantly\n\n### Files\n\n**Supported**: Any file type\n- Documents (PDF, Word, Excel)\n- Images (JPG, PNG, GIF)\n- Videos (MP4, MOV)\n- Archives (ZIP, RAR)\n- Code (any format)\n\n**Size**: No hard limit (browser memory dependent)\n\n**Transfer method**:\n- **Peer-to-peer** (P2P) when possible: Fast, direct\n- **Relay fallback**: Through server if P2P fails\n- **Automatic selection**: Tool picks best method\n\n### Multiple Items\n\n**Queue before connection**:\n- Type messages\n- Select files\n- All queued for sending\n- Auto-sent once connected\n\n**After connection**:\n- Send more at any time\n- Both directions work\n- No turn-taking needed\n\n## Security & Privacy\n\n### End-to-End Encryption Explained\n\n**Your device**:\n1. Generates encryption key pair\n2. Exchanges public key with peer\n3. Derives shared secret\n4. Encrypts data with shared secret\n5. Sends encrypted data\n\n**Server**:\n- Relays encrypted data\n- Cannot decrypt it\n- Doesn't store it\n\n**Receiver's device**:\n1. Receives encrypted data\n2. Decrypts with shared secret\n3. Displays original content\n\n**Result**: Only sender and receiver can read the data. Not even we can see it.\n\n### File Integrity\n\n**SHA-256 hashing**:\n- Each file gets hash before sending\n- Receiver verifies hash after download\n- Guarantees file arrived unchanged\n- Detects any corruption\n\n### Room Code Security\n\n**Random generation**: 1 million possible codes (000000-999999)\n\n**Temporary**: Codes expire when:\n- Devices disconnect\n- Room becomes inactive\n- Transfer completes\n\n**No reuse**: Each session gets new code\n\n**Collision protection**: Two people with same code at same time? Extremely unlikely (1 in 1M), and codes are time-limited.\n\n## Common Scenarios\n\n### Phone to Laptop Transfer\n\n**Situation**: Need laptop photo from phone\n\n**Steps**:\n1. Laptop: Open Share → Send\n2. Phone: Scan QR or enter code\n3. Phone: Select photo\n4. Laptop: Download received file\n5. Done in seconds\n\n### Collaboration at Meeting\n\n**Situation**: Share presentation file with attendees\n\n**Steps**:\n1. You: Create room, display code on screen\n2. Attendees: Enter code on their devices\n3. You: Send file once, all receive it\n4. Everyone has the file instantly\n\n### Remote File Sharing\n\n**Situation**: Send contract to colleague in another city\n\n**Steps**:\n1. You: Generate room code\n2. Text/email code to colleague (code alone is useless without file)\n3. Colleague: Enters code\n4. You: Send file\n5. Colleague: Downloads\n6. Delete message with code after transfer\n\n## Technical Details\n\n### Connection Methods\n\n**Peer-to-Peer (P2P)**:\n- WebRTC DataChannel\n- Direct device-to-device\n- Fastest (LAN: ~100 MB/s, Internet: varies)\n- Uses STUN servers for NAT traversal\n- Falls back if firewalls block\n\n**Relay Mode**:\n- Through WebSocket server\n- Used when P2P fails\n- Still encrypted end-to-end\n- Slower but reliable\n- Max chunk: 64KB (paced)\n\n**Auto-detection**: Tool tries P2P first, falls back to relay if needed within 10 seconds.\n\n### Browser Compatibility\n\nWorks on:\n- Chrome/Edge 90+\n- Firefox 88+\n- Safari 14+\n- Mobile browsers (iOS Safari, Chrome Android)\n\n**Requirements**:\n- JavaScript enabled\n- WebRTC support (all modern browsers)\n- Stable internet connection\n\n## FAQ\n\n### Is this really free?\n\nYes. No trials, no hidden fees, no paid tiers. Free forever.\n\n### Do I need an account?\n\nNo. No email, no signup, no login. Just visit and share.\n\n### Are my files stored anywhere?\n\nNo. Files transfer directly between devices (or through encrypted relay). Nothing stored on servers.\n\n### Can you see my files?\n\nNo. End-to-end encryption means only you and your recipient can decrypt the data.\n\n### What if we disconnect during transfer?\n\nYou'll need to restart. Files don't persist after disconnection. This is intentional for privacy.\n\n### Can I send to multiple people?\n\nCurrently supports two devices per room (sender and receiver). For groups, send to one person and they forward.\n\n### Is there a file size limit?\n\nNo artificial limit. Practical limit is browser memory (typically several GB). Large files take longer.\n\n### What happens to the room code after?\n\nRoom expires when you disconnect. Code becomes invalid and gets recycled.\n\n### Can someone guess my room code?\n\nUnlikely (1 in 1 million). And codes expire quickly. And even if someone joins, they'd need the encryption key exchange to happen, which you'd notice.\n\n### Does it work offline?\n\nNo, both devices need internet to find each other and connect. LAN-only mode isn't supported.\n\n## Troubleshooting\n\n### \"Waiting for peer\" stuck\n\n- **Check code**: Receiver entered correctly?\n- **Internet**: Both devices online?\n- **Refresh**: Reload page on both devices, try new room\n\n### Transfer very slow\n\n- **Check connection**: Wifi vs cellular data\n- **Relay mode**: P2P may have failed, relay is slower\n- **Large file**: Normal for big files on slow connections\n\n### \"Connection failed\"\n\n- **Firewall**: Corporate/school networks may block WebRTC\n- **VPN**: Try disabling temporarily\n- **Browser**: Update to latest version\n\n## Best Practices\n\n### For Security\n\n✅ **Do**:\n- Share room codes privately (voice, secure message)\n- Verify recipient joined (watch \"Connected\" status)\n- Disconnect after transfer\n- Use for one-time shares\n\n❌ **Don't**:\n- Post room codes publicly\n- Leave room open longer than needed\n- Reuse codes (tool doesn't allow this anyway)\n\n### For Speed\n\n- **Same WiFi network**: Much faster (LAN speeds)\n- **Good internet**: 4G/5G or broadband\n- **One file at a time**: For large files\n- **Compress first**: ZIP large folders\n\n### For Convenience\n\n- **QR codes**: Fastest for nearby devices\n- **Queue messages**: Type before receiver joins\n- **Both directions**: Anyone can send after connected\n\n## Alternatives Comparison\n\n### Email\n- ❌ Attachment limits (25MB typical)\n- ❌ Requires accounts\n- ❌ Files stored on servers\n- ✅ Good for async\n\n### Cloud Storage (Drive, Dropbox)\n- ❌ Requires account\n- ❌ Files stored (privacy concern)\n- ❌ Sharing link stays active\n- ✅ Good for persistence\n\n### USB Drive\n- ❌ Requires physical access\n- ❌ Slower for many files\n- ✅ Works offline\n- ✅ No size limits\n\n### AirDrop (Apple)\n- ✅ Fast and easy\n- ❌ Apple devices only\n- ❌ Requires physical proximity\n- ✅ Encrypted\n\n### Our Tool\n- ✅ Free, no account\n- ✅ Cross-platform\n- ✅ End-to-end encrypted\n- ✅ Remote or local\n- ✅ No storage\n- ❌ Requires both online\n- ❌ No persistence\n\n## Conclusion\n\nSending files without signing up is:\n- **Instant**: No registration delay\n- **Secure**: End-to-end encrypted\n- **Simple**: Six digits or QR code\n- **Private**: Nothing stored\n- **Free**: Always\n\nPerfect for:\n- Quick one-time transfers\n- Privacy-sensitive files\n- Cross-platform sharing\n- Meeting collaborations\n- Emergency file access\n\nTry our free Share tool now — no account needed."
